        "text": "if statement",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "definition_text": {
        "text": "a conditional statement that has three clauses or sections: the if clause, the else‑if clause, and the else clause",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "context": null
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "text": "brace (curly brace)",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "definition_text": {
        "text": "a pair of curly brackets { } that delimit a block of one or more statements; required only when there are multiple statements in a clause",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "context": null
    }
  ],
  "examples": [],
  "explanations": [
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "when to use braces in an if statement",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "braces are only required if a clause contains multiple statements; some developers always add them for consistency, while others omit them for single‑statement clauses to reduce visual noise",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "formatting of clauses after removing braces",
        "refs": ["Q0002", "Q0003"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "after removing unnecessary braces, the else‑if and else clauses should be placed on new lines at the same indentation level as the if clause to keep the code readable and symmetrical",
        "refs": ["Q0002", "Q0003"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "if a clause contains a single statement, braces may be omitted",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "removing unnecessary braces can simplify code formatting",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "the else‑if clause is typically indented slightly more than the if clause, while the else clause is at the same level as the if clause, which can look uneven",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    }
  ],
